1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 320 people. Revenue per employee of $2.3M ranks in the below the sector median among Real Estate peers, with revenue growing 46%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $37K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Phillips Edison & Company, Inc. is a mid-cap real estate business with a $5.8B market cap on $727M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +8% over the past three years and +12% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at -10% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 8.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.7% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 79% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.785920399380314},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Real Estate peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.2% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"(PECO) Risk Channels and Responsive Allocation","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/134/PECO_Risk_Channels_and_Responsive_Allocation_111226115801_1794545881.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794545881.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.202,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Phillips Edison & Company, Inc. (NASDAQ:PECO) Stock Gets Price Target Boost from UBS Group","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/phillips-edison-company-inc-nasdaqpeco-stock-gets-price-target-boost-from-ubs-group.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794433011.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.718,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Phillips Edison declares $0.115 dividend (NASDAQ:PECO)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4670587-phillips-edison-declares-0_115-dividend","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794399291.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Curbline Properties (NYSE:CURB) & Phillips Edison & Company, Inc. (NASDAQ:PECO) Critical Analysis","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/09/curbline-properties-nysecurb-phillips-edison-compa